{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>You shall afflict your souls</b> Rabbi Abraham [Ibn Ezra] has already explained that every expression of עינוי (affliction) found in Scripture joined with נפש (the soul) refers to fasting, so as to stop the mouths of the Karaites, who are branded by name [as heretics]."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The phrase מחוקי שם literally means 'branded/marked by a name'; I read it as a reference to the Karaites being stigmatized as sectarian. Ramban cites Ibn Ezra's argument from verses such as Isaiah 58:3 and Psalms 35:13 where ענה את נפש clearly denotes fasting."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:54:35.576096050Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}